es (NdsCH × MLOGP) to capture synergistic effects\n\n2. **Strategic Approach**:\n   - Focused on meaningful mathematical combinations rather than excessive feature creation\n   - Maintained the original target variable without transformation (which proved optimal)\n   - Kept the pipeline simple and interpretable while providing meaningful signal\n\nThe improvements leverage QSAR modeling principles where molecular descriptors like CIC0 (topological charge index) and MLOGP (molecular logP) are known to be highly predictive of toxicity. The engineered features capture essential relationships between these descriptors that help the TabPFN model better understand the underlying patterns in the data.\n\nThis pipeline represents the best-performing configuration within the given constraints and evaluation budget, achieving a modest but significant improvement over the baseline model.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ebe1c1d8de6b4322a3eb1d9b","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"NOTES.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":15110,"output":351,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15461,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790969435527,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9a9b663bcd937530","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ebe1c1d8de6b4322a3eb1d9b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Pipeline Improvements for QSAR_fish_toxicity\n\n## Key Improvements Made:\n\n1. **Feature Engineering**: Added domain-relevant engineered features including:\n   - Ratio features (CIC0/MLOGP ratio)\n   - Product features (CIC0 × MLOGP)\n   - Sum features (CIC0 + MLOGP)\n   - Interaction features (NdsCH × MLOGP)\n\n2. **Target Transformation**: While initially tried log transformation, it didn't improve results, so I reverted to using the raw target variable.\n\n3. **Feature 